sequenceDiagram
  accTitle: UCP identity linking: OAuth 2.0 authorization code with PKCE
  accDescr: Sequence diagram: UCP identity linking: OAuth 2.0 authorization code with PKCE. 3 participants: Buyer, Platform (agent surface), and Business (merchant of record). 7 steps, 7 crossing a trust boundary, 3 failure branches. Based on ucp 2026-08-25 (2026-08-25). Step 1: Platform (agent surface) to Business (merchant of record): GET /.well-known/oauth-protected-resource. This step crosses a trust boundary. Step 2: Platform (agent surface) to Business (merchant of record): GET /.well-known/oauth-authorization-server. This step crosses a trust boundary. If Issuer mismatch: The platform must stop the metadata may be spoofed. Step 3: Platform (agent surface) to Buyer: Redirect to authorize (PKCE S256, capability scopes). This step crosses a trust boundary. Step 4: Buyer to Business (merchant of record): Sign in and consent at the business. This step crosses a trust boundary. Step 5: Business (merchant of record) to Platform (agent surface): Redirect with code and iss. This step crosses a trust boundary. Step 6: Platform (agent surface) to Business (merchant of record): Token request with code_verifier. This step crosses a trust boundary. Step 7: Platform (agent surface) to Business (merchant of record): User-authenticated call, e.g. GET /orders/ id. This step crosses a trust boundary. If No user token: identity_required (401) with a WWW-Authenticate Bearer challenge. If Token lacks the scope: insufficient_scope (403).
  autonumber
  participant p_buyer as Buyer
  participant p_platform as Platform (agent surface)
  participant p_business as Business (merchant of record)
  p_platform->>p_business: GET /.well-known/oauth-protected-resource
  Note over p_platform,p_business: Crosses a trust boundary
  alt Expected path
    p_platform->>p_business: GET /.well-known/oauth-authorization-server
    Note over p_platform,p_business: Crosses a trust boundary
  else Issuer mismatch
    Note over p_platform,p_business: The platform must stop#59; the metadata may be spoofed.
  end
  p_platform->>p_buyer: Redirect to authorize (PKCE S256, capability scopes)
  Note over p_platform,p_buyer: Crosses a trust boundary
  p_buyer->>p_business: Sign in and consent at the business
  Note over p_buyer,p_business: Crosses a trust boundary
  p_business->>p_platform: Redirect with code and iss
  Note over p_business,p_platform: Crosses a trust boundary
  p_platform-->>p_business: Token request with code_verifier
  Note over p_platform,p_business: Crosses a trust boundary
  alt Expected path
    p_platform->>p_business: User-authenticated call, e.g. GET /orders/#123;id#125;
    Note over p_platform,p_business: Crosses a trust boundary
  else No user token
    Note over p_platform,p_business: identity_required (401) with a WWW-Authenticate Bearer challenge.
  else Token lacks the scope
    Note over p_platform,p_business: insufficient_scope (403).
  end
